   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** — head d661fa4\n\n1. **Medium**, `reader.css:342`, test `ReaderAllowlistContrastWebTests.swift:24`. The trailer's count bubble (`.quoted-bubble`: background `--secondary`, text `--background`) is not covered; a continuation's trailer can carry it. Its 75 % fade puts it at 3.15:1 light / 3.61 dark. The test passes `quotedByCount: nil`, so it never draws it. Fix: `.message.continuation .quoted-bubble { background: var(--secondary-faded); }` and `quotedByCount: 2` with a bubble ratio.\n2. **Low**, `reader.css:340`. The comment excludes the image link, the deleted note and the blocked summary with no issue tracking them (image link 3.15:1 light). Add the selectors (no cost) or open an issue.\n3. **Low**, outside #1360. The probe now reads the ordinary quote header of a classic allowlisted message that is not a continuation: `--secondary` on `--love` is 4.45:1 light (the #644 figure), asserted by nothing. A follow-up issue is enough.\n4. **Detail**, `reader.css:337-339`. \"2.8 to 3.4 on the worst surface\" is true for the quote header only; signature and trailer sit on the page (3.15 light / 3.61 dark). The suite doc comment does not mention #1360.\n\nRecomputed by the reviewer (probe formula, every surface: page, love 40 %, classic love, modo; light, Doux, dark `#2e2f33`, `#3a3b40`, `#1c1c1e`, black, Noël): after the fix ≥ 5.03 light, ≥ 5.67 dark (comment's 5.0 / 5.7 true); before the fix 2.80 to 4.12, so every new test fails without the change. Cascade OK (`.message.continuation b.s1` (0,3,1) vs folded-header rules (0,4,4), which keep `--text`; the author link keeps `--text`; #1210 dark date untouched). Every probed element exists in all three roots. `swiftc -swift-version 6 -typecheck` on a reduced copy passes, `swiftlint --strict` clean. Hosted WebKit tests not run (Linux).\n\nRound 1 fixes (one commit): 1 — bubble rule + `quotedByCount: 2` + `seen[6]` asserted; 2 — `.image-link`, `.deleted-note`, `.blocked-summary` added to the rule (same colour and surface; no hosted test draws them, said in the comment); 3 — follow-up #1362 opened; 4 — comment corrected, suite doc comment updated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
