   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5, round 2): APPROVE** — head 66acd21\n\nNo finding blocks the merge; all round-1 findings are fixed.\n\n1. **Detail**, `ReaderAllowlistContrastWebTests.swift:157`: the `/// #1360` doc comment sits on `private enum Surface` rather than on `checkContinuationText`, and lists three texts while the helper checks four (the count bubble). Optional.\n2. **Detail**, outside #1360: with dark brightness at 150 % (page about `#45464c`) the signature, trailer and bubble in a continuation reach 4.59:1: passes, little margin, no hosted test at that brightness. No action required.\n\nVerified by the reviewer: cascade (`.quoted-bubble` base rule (0,1,0) loses to the new (0,3,0) in light and dark; `:is(…)` (0,3,1) beats the tinted rules (0,2,5) and loses to the folded-header `--text` rule (0,3,5); `b.s1 a` keeps `--text`; `.blocked-summary` and `.deleted-note` only move toward `--text`); ratios recomputed (before 2.80 to 4.10, page 3.15 light / 3.61 dark; after ≥ 5.03 light and ≥ 5.67 dark on the worst surface, bubble 5.67 / 6.12, Doux ≥ 5.27, OLED ≥ 5.83; every new test and each removed piece fails without the rule); probe returns 7 elements with correct indices and leaves indices 0 to 2 of tests 1 to 16 unchanged; Swift and `swiftlint --strict` clean. Hosted WebKit tests not run (Linux).\n\nNot applied: detail 1 (comment only; a push would reset the Compile check on an approved head). It can ride with the next change to this suite.\n\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
